whisper: Lesson 2: Remembering things
whisper:
whisper: "set ... to ..." puts a value away under a name, so you can use it later.
whisper: Names can be more than one word, like "best score". That's on purpose.
whisper:
whisper: Inside quotes, a name in square brackets gets swapped for what it holds.
whisper: Run this and look at the second line closely.
whisper:
whisper: Your turn: add a line that sets coins to coins plus 10, then say how many there are now.

genesis:
  set name to "Sam"
  set coins to 3
  scrawl "This is ", name, "."
  scrawl "[name] has [coins] coins."
and the universe said i love you
